# Production data - never commit. Contains part numbers, customer-identifiable
# family names, work order numbers and actual job durations.
*.xlsx
*.parquet
*.csv

# Analysis outputs (regenerated from the extract). The per-operation
# workbooks moved out of the root on 2026-08-28 - 188 of the 214 entries
# that used to sit there - into `outputs/`, renamed outputs_run_pcs_hr/ on
# 2026-09-10 so the folder names its one run type. BOTH names are listed,
# and the patterns are kept as well as the folders: a gitignore pattern with
# no slash matches at any depth, so they cover both, and a stray workbook
# written to the root - or to the old folder - by an older copy of a script
# is still ignored rather than committed.
outputs_run_pcs_hr/
outputs/
FTS_*_PARTS.xlsx
FTS_*_FAMILY.xlsx
FTS_UPDATE_LIST.xlsx

# Superseded extracts, the queries that made them, and scope_changes.md.
# Local record only, and the WHOLE FOLDER is unpublishable, not just the
# parquets: scope_changes.md names families in plain prose. The identifier
# sweep in stage_for_github.py walks subfolders since 2026-09-02, but this
# folder is never staged in the first place - it is named in that script's
# SKIP_DIRS - so this line is what keeps it out, not the sweep.
archive/

# Local staging folder for the public repo
github_ready/

# Presentation material - prose, so the identifier sweep cannot help here.
# Names customers and quotes real durations throughout. Internal only.
H0_Presentation_*.md
H0_Presentation_*.pptx

# Review tool. Self-contained and read-only - it reads the workbooks and the
# parquet and writes nothing - so deleting the folder and this line removes
# every trace of it. Not published from THIS repo: the guided version has its
# own, staged by stage_streamlit_for_github.py.
streamlit_app/
github_ready_streamlit_app/

# IDE and tooling
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.iml
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
